     Project Management Domain (constituency-development-management)

     Context

     Following the decided plan in Doc/notes.txt (region hierarchy → fund → project → contractor → work-order/payment), the user asked to build Fund Management next.
     Fund Allocation, per the original spec (Doc/Prompt/Prompt, section 5), naturally targets a Project ("Temple A = 800,000"), but Project doesn't exist yet. When
     asked how to handle that dependency, the user chose to build Project Management first, then Fund on top of it with a real FK — avoiding a throwaway placeholder
     field.

     This plan covers Project Management only (Category → SubCategory → Project, with the priority-ranking queue described in section 4 of the spec). Fund Management
     follows in a subsequent step once this is in place.

     Source of truth for requirements

     Doc/Prompt/Prompt lines 104–184 (Development Category taxonomy, Project fields/status, Priority System) — this is the user's own spec from the original Claude
     prompt.

     Scope decisions (defaults applied, flag if you want different)

     - Location FK: Project.villageId — a single required FK to the existing Village entity (most granular level already built), same pattern as Member.constituencyId
     in member-management (one location FK, not multi-level).
     - Photos/documents: deferred. The spec calls for them but MinIO/S3 isn't wired into this repo yet — adding real file upload now would be a separate infra piece.
     Skipped for this pass.
     - Submitted by: stored as a plain String submittedBy (no cross-service FK to security-access-control's User).
     - Priority rank: stored as a plain field, kept in sync via an explicit recalculation endpoint (see below) rather than computed on every read — matches the manual,
     batch-driven workflow described in the spec (ranks get reset once a month when new projects are added to the queue).

     New entities (package com.himaloyit.buildnation.cdm.*, table prefix cons_)

     Category — cons_category: id, name, code (unique) — e.g. Education, Religious, Medical, Government Office, Communication, Agriculture, Water, Electricity, Social
     Welfare.

     SubCategory — cons_subcategory: id, name, code, category (@ManyToOne, FK) — e.g. Mosque, Temple, Primary School.

     Project — cons_project:
     - id, name, description, currentCondition (String)
     - category (@ManyToOne FK), subCategory (@ManyToOne FK), village (@ManyToOne FK)
     - estimatedCost (BigDecimal)
     - priorityScore (Integer, default 0), priorityRank (Integer, nullable — set by recalculation)
     - submittedBy (String)
     - status (ProjectStatus enum, default NEW)
     - createdAt, updatedAt (LocalDateTime, set manually)

     Enum domain/enums/ProjectStatus: NEW, PENDING_APPROVAL, APPROVED, ALLOCATED, RUNNING, INSPECTION, COMPLETED, CANCELLED (verbatim from spec section 3).

     Pattern to follow (mirror existing region-hierarchy slice exactly)

     Reference files already in the codebase:
     - Entity: domain/entities/Upazila.java (FK-to-parent pattern)
     - Mapper: domain/mapper/IUpazilaMapper.java (@Mapping(target = "xId", source = "x.id"))
     - Repository: domain/repositories/iRepositories/IUpazilaRepository.java
     - Service: services/impl/UpazilaService.java (constructor injection, @Cacheable/@CacheEvict/@CachePut with upazilas/upazilas-list cache names — no manual cache
     registration needed, RedisConfig uses dynamic cache names)
     - Controller: controllers/rest/UpazilaController.java (/create sub-path for POST, per repo convention)
     - Status/role PATCH pattern: member-management's MemberController.updateMemberStatus + UpdateMemberStatusRequest (@NotNull enum field)

     For each of Category, SubCategory, Project, create the same file set: domain/entities, domain/dto, domain/mapper (I*Mapper), domain/model (Create/Update requests),
     domain/repositories/iRepositories (I*Repository), services/iServices + services/impl, controllers/rest.

     Project-specific additions beyond plain CRUD

     ProjectController (/api/v1/projects), in addition to create/get/list/update/delete:
     - PATCH /{id}/status + UpdateProjectStatusRequest (@NotNull ProjectStatus status) — mirrors UpdateMemberStatusRequest
     - PATCH /{id}/priority + UpdateProjectPriorityRequest (@NotNull Integer priorityScore) — sets score only; rank is derived
     - GET /by-status/{status} (paginated) — mirrors getMembersByStatus
     - GET /by-category/{categoryId} (paginated)
     - GET /priority-queue?categoryId=&page=&size= — paginated, ordered by priorityRank ascending (nulls last), optional category filter — implements the "ranked queue"
     from spec section 4
     - POST /priority-queue/recalculate?categoryId= — service method: fetches projects with status in {NEW, PENDING_APPROVAL, APPROVED} (optionally filtered by
     category), sorts by priorityScore descending, writes back priorityRank 1..N, evicts relevant caches. Directly implements the spec's core scenario ("100 temples
     ranked, fund only reaches the top 10").

     ICategoryRepository/ISubCategoryRepository/IProjectRepository: add findByCategoryId, and for Project a native/derived query for the recalculation fetch
     (findByStatusInOrderByPriorityScoreDesc).

     CategoryController/SubCategoryController: plain CRUD only, same shape as DistrictController/UpazilaController.

